From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: track Elden host power loss across system suspend

Extend the existing Freedom host power-loss handling from Baldur to Elden.
Elden resumes with a USB SID 0x40 SMMU translation fault followed by an
xHCI Host System Error after the controller was powered down. Switching
USB roles tears down and recreates xHCI, allowing the G9 to enumerate
again.

Track the existing core-exit decision and pass it to xHCI on resume, so it
resets lost state. Keep the existing retention path when the core stays on.

Based-on: armadaos-freedom 244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0192-usb-baldur-runtime-pm.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2616,12 +2616,14 @@
 		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg) &&
 		    (!device_may_wakeup(dwc->dev) || dwc->needs_full_reinit)) {
 			dwc3_core_exit(dwc);
-			if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+			if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") ||
+			    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden"))
 				dwc->xhci_power_lost = 1;
 			break;
 		}
 
-		if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") ||
+		    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden"))
 			dwc->xhci_power_lost = 0;
 
 		/* Let controller to suspend HSPHY before PHY driver suspends */
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -83,7 +83,8 @@
 {
 	struct dwc3 *dwc = dev_get_drvdata(hcd->self.controller->parent);
 
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") ||
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden"))
 		hcd_to_xhci_priv(hcd)->power_lost = dwc->xhci_power_lost;
 	return 0;
 }
